cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite the accompanying paper and this repository."
title: "StructuralSieve: a Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of an exact sieve-coverage characterization of primality"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked (zero-`sorry`) Lean 4 development proving two exact,
  unconditional characterizations of primality via sieve-coverage: on a prime
  base's own window (P_k, 2*P_k], and generalized to the base's full
  deterministic reach, the zone (P_k, P_k^2), with the reach shown exact.
  Bertrand's postulate is not the target of this development; it converges
  with it only as a corollary, since the base's window always contains a
  prime -- the same classical fact proved by Chebyshev (1852) and, via a
  different route, Erdos (1932). The corollary's own closure does not import
  Mathlib's proof of Bertrand's postulate.
type: software
authors:
